        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-06T08:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, good. This is pretty much what this does, so we should be good I think.\n\nWith MODULES_ORDER set, we basically compare the list of modules generated by the build (which is included in the modules.order build artifact) with the expected list of modules checked in the tree (which is essentially the modules.order resulting from a previous build). Any difference in these two lists will be reported as a fatal build error, and require a module list update which will have to be included in the kernel patch causing the change.\n\nThat should guarantee we don\u0027t compile modules accidentally because of an upstream or LTS change (see the parent of this patch for instance), and should be very low overhead to maintain as updating the module list is as simple as copying the new modules.order file in the right place.",
      "parentUuid": "57ef5a82_b10ec0af",
      "revId": "0939eda0346d0d08211b9b0d0a4efa8a164f19a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
